---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import Content from '~/components/widgets/Content.astro';
import Features3 from '~/components/widgets/Features3.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'The Enrollment Drop-Off Problem — Storyline Branching Scenario',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Hero tagline="Instructional Design · Articulate Storyline 360 · A/B Testing · GrowthBook SDK">
    <Fragment slot="title">
      The Enrollment Drop-Off Problem —<br />
      <span class="text-accent dark:text-white">A Branching Scenario for Launchpath Academy</span>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="subtitle">
      A corporate instructional design portfolio piece following the full design process — needs analysis, learning
      objectives, storyboard, and a Storyline 360 branching scenario built around A/B testing with GrowthBook SDK.
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <!-- Context -->
  <Content tagline="The Problem" title="34% of learners never complete enrollment" isReversed>
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-full py-12">
        <div class="text-center">
          <p class="text-7xl font-bold font-heading text-accent leading-none">34%</p>
          <p class="text-xl text-muted mt-3">Enrollment Drop-Off Rate</p>
          <div class="mt-8 space-y-2 text-sm text-muted">
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">Launchpath Academy · SaaS EdTech</p>
            <p>GrowthBook SDK · A/B Testing</p>
            <p>Articulate Storyline 360</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        Launchpath Academy is a growing SaaS edtech company whose revenue is directly tied to learner enrollment
        completion rates. Analytics revealed that 34% of learners who reached the enrollment confirmation page abandoned
        the process — a significant and measurable business problem.
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The suspected cause: CTA button copy reading "Complete Enrollment" felt final and intimidating rather than
        motivating. But the team had no evidence-based process for testing this hypothesis — they were making product
        decisions based on gut instinct rather than data.
      </p>
      <p>
        This module was designed to close that gap — giving L&D and product team members the knowledge and skills to
        design, implement, and interpret a proper A/B test using GrowthBook SDK.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 section-pattern-b"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Design Process -->
  <Features3
    tagline="Design Process"
    title="From problem to published module"
    subtitle="Following a full instructional design process — analysis, design, development, and evaluation planning."
    columns={3}
    items={[
      {
        title: 'Needs Analysis',
        description:
          'Identified the performance gap, root cause, and audience profile before writing a single learning objective. The 34% drop-off was a symptom — the root cause was a knowledge and skill gap in evidence-based product decision-making.',
        icon: 'tabler:search',
      },
      {
        title: 'Learning Objectives',
        description:
          "Four objectives written to Bloom's Taxonomy — progressing from Knowledge (define a testable hypothesis) through Application (configure GrowthBook) to Analysis (interpret results) and Synthesis (connect to business outcomes).",
        icon: 'tabler:target',
      },
      {
        title: 'Storyboard',
        description:
          'A full slide-by-slide storyboard documented before building — mapping each decision point, branching path, consequence screen, and debrief to specific learning objectives.',
        icon: 'tabler:layout-board',
      },
      {
        title: 'Branching Scenario',
        description:
          'Built in Articulate Storyline 360 — three decision points mirroring the real A/B testing workflow. Wrong answers produce realistic consequence screens, not grade penalties. Learning from failure is more durable.',
        icon: 'tabler:git-branch',
      },
      {
        title: 'GrowthBook SDK Integration',
        description:
          'Decision 2 surfaces real GrowthBook SDK code — making the scenario concrete and tool-specific. Learners see what implementation actually looks like, not an abstraction.',
        icon: 'tabler:code',
      },
      {
        title: 'Kirkpatrick Evaluation',
        description:
          'Evaluation planned across all four levels — from post-module confidence ratings (Level 1) through behavioral follow-up on real product decisions (Level 3) to enrollment completion rate improvement (Level 4).',
        icon: 'tabler:chart-bar',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- Module Embed -->
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 py-12 md:py-16">
    <div class="text-center mb-10">
      <p class="text-base text-secondary dark:text-blue-200 font-bold tracking-wide uppercase mb-2">Storyline Module</p>
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter font-heading">Take the Scenario</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-muted mt-4">
        A branching Storyline 360 scenario — three decisions, real consequences, and a debrief connecting A/B testing to
        business outcomes at Launchpath Academy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="relative w-full rounded-lg shadow-lg overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800 flex items-center justify-center"
      style="min-height: 360px;"
    >
      <div class="text-center px-8 py-16">
        <div
          class="w-16 h-16 rounded-full bg-accent/10 dark:bg-accent/20 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-5"
        >
          <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-accent" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor">
            <path d="M8 5v14l11-7z"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <p class="text-2xl font-bold font-heading text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200 mb-2">Module Coming Soon</p>
        <p class="text-muted text-base max-w-md mx-auto">
          The Storyline module is currently in development. Check back shortly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Learning Objectives -->
  <Content tagline="Learning Design" title="Objectives written to Bloom's Taxonomy" isReversed>
    <Fragment slot="image">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-full py-12 px-6">
        <div class="w-full max-w-xs space-y-3">
          {
            [
              {
                label: 'Define a testable hypothesis',
                detail: 'Knowledge — framing the right question',
                color: 'blue',
              },
              { label: 'Configure the experiment', detail: 'Application — GrowthBook SDK setup', color: 'green' },
              { label: 'Interpret the results', detail: 'Analysis — p-value and lift percentage', color: 'purple' },
              { label: 'Connect to business outcomes', detail: 'Synthesis — data-driven decisions', color: 'orange' },
            ].map(({ label, detail, color }) => (
              <div
                class={`flex items-start gap-3 p-2.5 rounded-lg border ${color === 'blue' ? 'border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-800 bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-900/20' : color === 'green' ? 'border-green-200 dark:border-green-800 bg-green-50 dark:bg-green-900/20' : color === 'purple' ? 'border-purple-200 dark:border-purple-800 bg-purple-50 dark:bg-purple-900/20' : 'border-orange-200 dark:border-orange-800 bg-orange-50 dark:bg-orange-900/20'}`}
              >
                <div>
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">{label}</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-muted mt-0.5">{detail}</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="content">
      <p class="mb-4">
        The four learning objectives follow a deliberate Bloom's Taxonomy progression — starting with defining a
        testable hypothesis (Knowledge), moving through configuring a real GrowthBook experiment (Application),
        interpreting statistical results (Analysis), and synthesizing the experience into a business decision
        (Synthesis).
      </p>
      <p class="mb-4">
        The most common failure mode in A/B testing isn't the implementation — it's the interpretation. Teams either
        ship too early (misreading noise as signal) or wait too long (not recognizing a clear win). Decision 3 is
        designed specifically to build that judgment.
      </p>
      <p>
        Evaluation is planned across all four Kirkpatrick levels — from immediate confidence ratings through behavioral
        follow-up to measurable improvement in Launchpath Academy's enrollment completion rate.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="bg">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 section-pattern"></div>
    </Fragment>
  </Content>

  <!-- Tags -->
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 md:px-8 pb-16">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      {
        [
          'Articulate Storyline 360',
          'Branching Scenario',
          'Needs Analysis',
          "Bloom's Taxonomy",
          'Kirkpatrick Model',
          'GrowthBook SDK',
          'A/B Testing',
          'Corporate ID',
          'Instructional Design',
          'ADDIE Process',
          'Storyboard',
          'SaaS EdTech',
        ].map((tag) => (
          <span class="bg-blue-100 dark:bg-blue-900 text-blue-800 dark:text-blue-200 text-sm font-medium px-3 py-1 rounded-full">
            {tag}
          </span>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
